  "description": "Go hard without breaking the bank\nSythe S delivers the confidence and control you need for steep, rough and demanding trails in a high value, high performance package: progressive, proportionally-sized geometry and capable long-travel Quad-Link 4 suspension keep handling stable and predictable when speeds rise and terrain gets technical, while balanced performance makes climbing back up feel efficient and manageable. Tough, dependable and dressed in trail-proven components, with weather-sealed durability and MX (mixed/'mullet') wheels for clearance when things get steep, Sythe S is designed for real-world riding, and ready to handle both year-round abuse and the biggest days on the hill alike.\n\nHighlights\n– 170mm front + 160mm rear of Whyte custom-tuned suspension travel (Marzocchi Bomber Z1 29in fork + Marzocchi Bomber Air piggyback rear shock).\n– 6061 hydroformed T6 multi-butted alloy frame + geometry adjustment.\n– Proportional sizing delivers perfect fit and uncompromised handling for every rider.\n– Shimano Deore 1x12 transmission (30T chainring x 10-52T cassette).\n– TRP EVO Comp four-piston hydraulic disc brakes (203mm rotors front + rear).\n– Full-insertion dropper post (with frame size size-specific drop).\n– MX/mixed/’mullet’ wheels (29in front, 27.5in rear) + Schwalbe Magic Mary Radial tyres (ready to be converted to full 29in front and rear (sizes M, L + XL only)).\n\nIdeal for... Gravity thrill seekers, enduro racers, bike-park shredders, and big mountain riders looking for top performance at a low price.",
